mpu:53215.description:
As the only academic honor society that confers recognition on eligible individuals from all engineering disciplines, Tau Beta Pi:
Recognizes those who have conferred honor upon their Alma Maters by distinguished scholarship and exemplary character as students in engineering, or by their attainments as alumni in the field of engineering;
Provides leadership and professional development training for engineering students and alumni members;
Promotes lifelong alumnus member involvement.
This organization is open to all Princeton University students interested in supporting our organization’s mission, regardless of identity, such as race, sex, ethnicity, national origin, or other protected characteristics.

mpu:71421.goals:
The Princeton Education Society proclaims that it has been founded to:
- Create a community hub for undergraduate students interested in education;
- Assist in the career development of students interested in education (primary and secondary schools, academia and research, non-profits, government, etc.), particularly by connecting undergraduate students with relevant alumni and other educational professionals;
- Engage with educational topics through practical action, broadly defined, including through local community projects, collaborations with educational service organizations at Princeton University, etc.

mpu:71691.description:
The Princeton Opera Society is dedicated to promote and encourage amongst its members:
1. The enjoyment and appreciation of opera as an art form;
2. Improving accessibility to the opera and challenging preconceptions about it;
3. Regular attendance of opera performances and related concert vocal music, both locally and farther afield;
4. Education about the various facets of opera, including from historical, theatrical, literary and musical perspectives;
5. Fellowship among opera enthusiasts and performers in the Princeton community.
